me enum extension).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.065,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope names only 'src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py' as an added file","terraform_seam.py:_session_tools currently returns [terraform_lookup_declaration, terraform_resolve_reference, terraform_probe_source]; a new tool must be added there for both pipelines to advertise it (code_review/terraform_grounding.py delegates to terraform_seam.build_tool_provider)","terraform_tools.py added probe_source as a session method in the prerequisite ticket; the same session-method edit is required here but unnamed","terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json outcome enum is currently [refuted, abstain] and operation enum lacks corroborate_diagnostic — both need editing per the plan's own prose ('corroborate_diagnostic joins the operation enum and match joins the outcome enum')"],"finding":"The plan's Scope enumerates only the new file src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py, but advertising a new session operation (per the pattern the depended-on ticket used for probe_source) requires editing four files OUTSIDE that directory that the plan never names as edit targets: src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py (add a corroborate_diagnostic session method), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py (_session_tools / build_tool_provider — the single shared minting site both pipelines consume), src/rebar/grounding/terraform_receipt.py (receipt construction + the ABSTENTIONS/outcome handling for the new match outcome), and src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json (extend the operation and outcome enums). AC6 asserts both pipelines advertise corroborate_diagnostic and the prose says the receipt schema is extended, but the edit set does not list the consumers required to realize either.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0e93efd18c780a5f","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('Add src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py and expose corroborate_diagnostic ... through established Terraform Pass-1 and Pass-2 sessions'); AC6","norm_id":"n03abe29dbe104dab","priority":0.765,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer builds the corroborator module but the tool never surfaces because _session_tools/build_tool_provider was not updated","Receipt validation fails at runtime because the schema outcome enum still rejects 'match'"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an explicit edit-target list to Scope naming src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py, src/rebar/grounding/terraform_receipt.py, and src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json, mirroring how the depended-on probe_source slice enumerated the same set of consumers.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how process termination/reaping and the snapshot-cleanup guarantee are achieved on Windows (or explicitly scope the corroborator to POSIX platforms and confirm Windows sessions simply never advertise the tool).","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Close stdin, create a process group/session, and allow only locale, OS-required process variables...'","Plan: 'On timeout, overflow, cancellation, or error, terminate then kill and reap the whole group and remove the snapshot.'","Windows is a named supported platform in the matrix; process groups/sessions and POSIX kill signals are unavailable there, and terraform-config-inspect ships as a cross-platform Go binary that can be on a Windows PATH."],"finding":"The hardened-execution contract specifies POSIX-only process control — 'create a process group/session' and 'terminate then kill and reap the whole group' — but terraform-config-inspect is a cross-platform Go binary that can appear on a Windows PATH; Windows has no setsid/process-group/SIGKILL semantics, so the launcher's reaping path is unspecified for the Windows platform where a user has the binary installed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa833fffe5cb8fb5a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Hardened execution ('Close stdin, create a process group/session ... terminate then kill and reap the whole group')","norm_id":"nc961b83a063347dc","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows developer workstation with terraform-config-inspect on PATH: the launcher's process-group/session creation and group-kill/reap has no Windows equivalent, so a corroboration invocation fails to launch or cannot terminate/reap on timeout — the corroborator errors instead of cleanly abstaining, or leaks the child, on a supported platform."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a portability note: either restrict the corroborator to POSIX platforms (